{"event_type":"review","id":"9b0d27428b86d207e9611a3a46aaab171464f3a078b5e944d9bae532242e9e02","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T18:15:17Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9c7c4c84f83bfcf39cb644ebb63c4333491fe68aa4626f5ecbdc8a613618c52e","sha256":"9c7c4c84f83bfcf39cb644ebb63c4333491fe68aa4626f5ecbdc8a613618c52e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0dc88f1f48f8683e2f2b746c7fec4d96a7e3d438277d752df1f8913462db1b36","sha256":"0dc88f1f48f8683e2f2b746c7fec4d96a7e3d438277d752df1f8913462db1b36"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5a5729a117051458418ed4db82104e95129cc90f93c6636dc68a4a1485bf5730","sha256":"5a5729a117051458418ed4db82104e95129cc90f93c6636dc68a4a1485bf5730"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f8aeea7a6ccf23f9804131d22b33cc832841ab4dc68648e808f02a8f87f69c90","sha256":"f8aeea7a6ccf23f9804131d22b33cc832841ab4dc68648e808f02a8f87f69c90"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0a3aa716d15959173615f0486a20d524079f0f8584ae5eef320e20cee5f023fb","sha256":"0a3aa716d15959173615f0486a20d524079f0f8584ae5eef320e20cee5f023fb"}],"attempt_id":"bfefce4d047e394a829169544282d118dbdeada7ac80973747bfaf55f1108e53:0:1","base":"64549c7bbeabe1fa079c35ac73e77b6203cddb37","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"f926be5c492c525da8d312b018df9a48bf43c44e","body":"**Mark the run file as dir-synced only after `syncDir` succeeds.**\n\nAt `src/kernel/journal.ts:883`, `dirSynced.add(runId)` runs before `await syncDir(journalDir)`. `syncDir` ignores only `EPERM`, `EACCES`, `EINVAL`, and `ENOSYS`. Any other error, such as `EIO`, propagates. When that happens, the append rejects, but the line is already in the file and `runId` is already in `dirSynced`. Every later append to that run then skips the directory fsync.\n\nThe `RunLog.append` contract at lines 816-818 promises one directory fsync for each new run file. That promise is not met after one failed sync, and nothing reports the gap. Durable `reservation-*` lines can then sit in a file whose directory entry was never made durable.\n\nRecord the run ID only after the directory sync succeeds. A failed sync then gets another attempt on the next append.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         if (isNew) {\n-          dirSynced.add(runId);\n           await syncDir(journalDir);\n+          dirSynced.add(runId);\n         }\n```\n</details>","id":"a60911158a1147644facde41413210f9238e79cd062deea09b6389f1b67de6fa","intervals":[],"path":"src/kernel/journal.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Mark the run file as dir-synced only after `syncDir` succeeds."}],"head":"c8127d32cf4457939c88c149a19e3e8f00db50e7","head_tree":"e04fe6b46a2a7a3ff99e793e23ea2c0b8de4edf9","input_scope":[{"blob":"f926be5c492c525da8d312b018df9a48bf43c44e","intervals":[[8,10],[24,46],[65,773],[786,787],[813,819],[821,821],[844,847],[850,850],[853,860],[867,867],[870,885],[921,1141],[1175,1175],[1179,1202],[1214,1233],[1267,1267],[1319,1341]],"path":"src/kernel/journal.ts"},{"blob":"acf0678d1888f11f14d8f224d928f9f42f808bd5","intervals":[[26,26],[28,36],[42,42],[45,45],[47,47],[52,82],[86,91],[94,111],[134,207],[221,226],[228,235],[237,243],[245,267],[269,283],[285,334],[337,349],[351,359],[361,371],[395,399],[401,460],[462,472],[474,515],[517,608],[628,1341],[1346,1380]],"path":"src/kernel/schema.ts"}],"job_id":"bfefce4d047e394a829169544282d118dbdeada7ac80973747bfaf55f1108e53:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"efdd989a9156e5a533a16400dcbf6bfd2770c595","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/kernel/journal.ts"},"merge":"6a842e1e1bf6ffde44dd9d8f561a01d702b4bb34","method":"pre-merge","pre":"5170bdc4c98ac6712fb87c0109c31445488629f1","source_path":"src/ke